WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.703
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Friday, November twenty seventh.

2
00:00:04.703 --> 00:00:14.039
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:14.968
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:31.246
Today: two Italian workers killed in a drone attack in Kuwait, a deadly strike on a Saudi refinery in Jazan, a deadly night raid in Nigeria's Plateau State, arrests in Germany over a synagogue bomb plot, and new Australian sanctions over Iran-directed arson attacks.

5
00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:32.617
We start in Kuwait.

6
00:00:32.617 --> 00:00:40.520
Reuters reports two Italian workers were killed in an attack on a site in Kuwait yesterday, with a source saying it was an Iranian strike.

7
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:48.961
Al Jazeera reports Kuwait confirmed the deaths, and the Italian news agency ANSA says the two worked for the German defense company Rheinmetall.

8
00:00:48.961 --> 00:00:56.632
Iran's foreign minister, Abbas Araghchi, rejected claims that Tehran was behind the attack and called the incident suspicious.

9
00:00:56.632 --> 00:00:58.374
Turning to Saudi Arabia.

10
00:00:58.374 --> 00:01:05.151
Reuters reports an attack on Saudi Aramco's Jazan refinery killed a worker and halted some operations yesterday.

11
00:01:05.151 --> 00:01:16.018
Al Jazeera, citing Saudi Arabia's energy ministry, says the worker was a Nepali national and that others were injured, and the Saudi-led coalition said the Houthis carried out the attack.

12
00:01:16.018 --> 00:01:17.694
Next, Nigeria.

13
00:01:17.694 --> 00:01:29.334
TheCable and THISDAY report gunmen killed at least sixteen people in an overnight attack on the Tafi Gana community near Miango, in Bassa Local Government Area of Plateau State, on Wednesday night.

14
00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:37.620
Local media report the state government put the toll at seven killed and three injured, and that the governor directed security agencies to respond.

15
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.951
The Tracking Terrorism and Counter Extremism group attributes the attack to Fulani herdsmen.

16
00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:53.233
In Germany, federal prosecutors say police arrested two Iraqi nationals in Heidelberg and Cologne yesterday on suspicion of membership in a pro-Iranian terrorist group.

17
00:01:53.233 --> 00:02:06.203
Prosecutors say the group recruited people for bomb attacks, and that in late March unknown suspects, presumably carrying explosives, went to synagogues in Cologne and another European city, but no attack was carried out.

18
00:02:06.203 --> 00:02:12.272
Deutsche Welle reports more than two hundred fifty officers took part in searches at seventeen locations.

19
00:02:12.272 --> 00:02:23.428
And in Australia, Reuters reports the government placed counterterrorism financing sanctions on two people it said orchestrated antisemitic arson attacks in Sydney and Melbourne on behalf of Iran.

20
00:02:23.428 --> 00:02:25.622
Now a few quick notes by region.

21
00:02:25.622 --> 00:02:32.109
In Europe, Australia's Smartraveller says Estonia will close its border crossings with Russia from December first.

22
00:02:32.109 --> 00:02:39.351
Reuters reports a drone briefly violated Latvian airspace, according to Latvia's armed forces.

23
00:02:39.351 --> 00:02:47.716
Off Ibiza, Reuters reports a crew member died after a diesel tanker capsized, and Spanish authorities are working to contain any spill.

24
00:02:47.716 --> 00:02:56.818
In Africa, Canada's travel advisory service says the Gambia holds general elections on December fifth and demonstrations could occur before, during and after the vote.

25
00:02:56.818 --> 00:02:57.804
The U.K.

26
00:02:57.804 --> 00:03:03.494
Foreign Office updated its Mauritius advice with information about local demonstrations.

27
00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:12.099
In Egypt, Al Jazeera reports a fuel tanker overturned and caught fire on a Cairo highway, killing thirty one people, and prosecutors detained the driver.

28
00:03:12.099 --> 00:03:22.145
And in an update on Ebola, Reuters reports a Kenyan court ruled the government breached the constitution by allowing a U.S.-backed Ebola quarantine site at a military air base.

29
00:03:22.145 --> 00:03:34.158
In the Middle East, Al Jazeera reports Iran's army navy commander said Iranian forces recovered two Iranian oil tankers he said had been seized by the U.S. military, according to Iranian state media.

30
00:03:34.158 --> 00:03:36.176
The U.S. has not commented.

31
00:03:36.176 --> 00:03:43.843
The I C R C says it facilitated the transfer of human remains across front lines in Yemen from November twenty fourth to twenty sixth.

32
00:03:43.843 --> 00:03:53.331
In Asia, T R T World reports a crude bomb exploded outside a court in Dhaka, Bangladesh, injuring a lawyer, and police detained a suspect.

33
00:03:53.331 --> 00:04:01.426
In Latin America, Reuters reports, citing sources, that a fire prompted the evacuation of workers at Venezuela's Amuay refinery.

34
00:04:01.426 --> 00:04:08.163
In the Pacific, Smartraveller says Vanuatu's health ministry declared an influenza A outbreak in Port Vila and on Efate Island.

35
00:04:08.163 --> 00:04:15.061
On cyber, Reuters reports Standard Chartered's crypto unit, Zodia Custody, was hit by a security breach that exposed some client data.

36
00:04:15.061 --> 00:04:25.234
Reuters also reports India's Election Commission fixed a website flaw that exposed some voters' personal details, after Reuters alerted it.

37
00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:26.915
That's today's brief.

38
00:04:26.915 --> 00:04:36.459
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

39
00:04:36.459 --> 00:04:44.624
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

40
00:04:44.624 --> 00:04:46.758
This brief is digitally narrated.

41
00:04:46.758 --> 00:04:47.712
Questions?

42
00:04:47.712 --> 00:04:51.119
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

43
00:04:51.119 --> 00:04:53.148
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
